The invention relates to a method for producing and deburring toothings on workpieces (6), the method employing two workpiece spindles (3, 3′), a hobbing tool (12), and a deburring device (10). The workpieces (6) are automatically clamped into the workpiece spindles (3, 3′), toothed by means of the hobbing tool (12), and subsequently deburred. The method comprises the following steps:

a. receiving an unmachined workpiece (6) in a first loading position (19) by means of a first workpiece spindle (3) and transporting the workpiece (6) to the hobbing tool (12);

b. carrying out a milling cut;

c. depositing the workpiece (6) in the first loading position (19) and receiving a further unmachined workpiece (6);

d. transporting the workpiece (6) machined by the milling cut to a second loading position (19′);

e. receiving the workpiece (6) in the second loading position (19′) by means of the second workpiece spindle (3′) and transporting the workpiece (6) to the deburring tool (10);

f. deburring the workpiece (6),

wherein an intermediate storage unit (14) for at least one workpiece (6) is provided between the first loading position (19) and the second loading position (19′), wherein the workpiece (6) is moved from the intermediate storage unit (14) into the second loading position (19′), and wherein method steps e. and f. are carried out within the same time interval as method step b.

