1. A method for producing and deburring gear toothings on workpieces, the method comprising:

providing a gear-cutting machine comprising a first workpiece spindle, a second workpiece spindle, a hobbing tool, a deburring device, at least one loading position, and an intermediate storage for workpieces;

loading a first workpiece onto the first workpiece spindle at a first loading position;

machining the first workpiece on the first workpiece spindle with the hobbing tool to produce a gear toothing on the first workpiece;

transferring the first workpiece, after said machining, from the first workpiece spindle to the intermediate storage;

loading a second workpiece onto the second workpiece spindle at a second loading position;

deburring, by means of the deburring device, the gear toothing of a workpiece held on one of the first and second workpiece spindles; and

hobbing, by means of the hobbing tool, another workpiece held on the other of the first and second workpiece spindles,

wherein the hobbing of the another workpiece and the deburring of the gear toothing of the workpiece are performed at least partially simultaneously, and wherein workpieces are transferred between the loading position, the first and second workpiece spindles, and the intermediate storage such that a workpiece having a hobbed gear toothing is temporarily stored in the intermediate storage before being supplied to one of the first and second workpiece spindles for deburring.

1. A method of producing toothings on workpieces in a gear-cutting machine comprising two workpiece spindles (3, 3′), a hobbing tool (12), a deburring tool (10), first and second loading positions (19, 19′), and an intermediate storage device (14), the method comprising the following steps:

a) loading a first workpiece at the first loading position (19) onto a first workpiece spindle (3);

b) moving the first workpiece spindle (3) with the first workpiece into a machining position and producing a toothing on the first workpiece by milling with the hobbing tool (12);

c) during the milling of the first workpiece, loading a second workpiece at the second loading position (19′) onto a second workpiece spindle (3′);

d) after completion of the milling of the first workpiece, transferring the first workpiece spindle (3) or the first workpiece into an engagement position with the deburring tool (10) and deburring the toothing of the first workpiece;

e) while the first workpiece is being deburred by the deburring tool (10), moving the second workpiece spindle (3′) with the second workpiece into the machining position and producing a toothing on the second workpiece by milling with the hobbing tool (12), such that deburring of one workpiece is carried out simultaneously with milling of another workpiece; and

f) unloading a machined and deburred workpiece from one of the workpiece spindles (3, 3′) at one of the loading positions (19, 19′) or depositing the machined and deburred workpiece in the intermediate storage device (14), and subsequently loading a further workpiece from the intermediate storage device (14) or from one of the loading positions (19, 19′) onto the respective workpiece spindle (3, 3′),

wherein the two workpiece spindles (3, 3′) are operated in an alternating cycle so that, during continuous production, milling by the hobbing tool (12) on a workpiece held by one workpiece spindle and deburring by the deburring tool (10) on a previously milled workpiece held by the other workpiece spindle take place at least partially simultaneously.
